    {
      "id": "claim_2f05523c55e4494f91e455da3c2b3091",
      "statement": "packages/server/src/database/index.ts exports initializeDatabase() which, on every server startup, first calls applyStagedRestore() to check for BACKUP_DIR/restore-pending.json before the database file is even opened; if the marker is absent it proceeds with a normal boot, and if present it validates both stagedDbPath and targetDbPath (rejecting NUL bytes, '..', or backslashes as path traversal) and requires the staged file to exist before atomically renaming it over the live database path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/database/index.ts#L36-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09edc9ef0cd26cfb8462618a667df8c90e33859f26e54b7beb449e7f5af969f9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/database/index.ts#L89-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79d85a4eca6a3cade28ebc7f617f96ac0404255d4b81ba13957ddbe007f78a37:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73f32612aa02490f9740159ceeab95d4",
      "statement": "If restore-marker validation fails (invalid marker, path traversal, or missing staged file), applyStagedRestore() renames the marker to 'restore-pending.json.failed' and leaves the current database untouched, preventing an invalid restore from retrying on every boot or partially applying.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/server/src/database/index.ts#L43-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77f238aa8847a37f84ae122c0f221376e5f49445a4dccfb8bccc0218b505b107:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_458c9ded192c49e398cc8135ef541b56",
      "statement": "After opening the database with foreign_keys=ON and journal_mode=WAL, initializeDatabase() runs runPreSchemaMigrations(db) before executing the schema and explainerSchema SQL strings, because CREATE INDEX statements in schema.ts reference columns that must already exist on stale pre-existing tables (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS cannot retroactively add columns).",
