    {
      "id": "claim_46440570017945b28e40f82d40dcb399",
      "statement": "migrate.ts provides addMissingColumns(db, table, columns), which reads PRAGMA table_info and issues ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN only for columns missing on an already-existing table, and is a no-op when the table does not yet exist (because CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS will create it fresh with all columns) — this is the general pattern used by dozens of createPhaseNN*Tables() functions to keep older databases in sync with newer schema shapes.",
